    "Fumi was dextrous through every step of the process; compared to her, Hina was awkward."

    "It was natural for there to be a difference between them, since Fumi had been taught the basics by her patissier father since she was little, and Hina was doing this for the first time."

    "She was trying to mix fresh cream and corn syrup into the chocolate, but was having a hard time."

